Changes to cipher.go (all mechanical; work/volume-parity/vendor-src/cipher.diff shows them):
  - package crypt -> package rclonecrypt; a header comment;
  - imports: pkcs7, version and eme from the vendored subpackages; rclone's fs, accounting and readers dropped;
  - fs.RangeSeeker -> rangeSeeker (shims.go, the same interface); fs.Errorf -> logf (a no-op);
    accounting.UnWrap -> unWrap (identity: no accounting here); readers.ReadFill -> readFill (verbatim);
  - NewNameEncoding loses its "base32768" case (the github.com/Max-Sum/base32768 dependency). encVolumes never sets a
    filename encoding: rclone's default base32 is always used, unchanged.
pkcs7, version and eme are verbatim apart from a one-line origin comment. api.go is NOT rclone's: the constructor rclone's
crypt backend performs (New), a fixed-nonce EncryptData (EncryptDataNonce, for hash-then-send) and Forget (zero the keys).
Compatibility is tested both ways against the pinned rclone v1.67.0 binary (encvol/compat_test.go).
